# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PortalVault .gitignore
#
# Security rule: secrets and internal legacy data must never reach this
# repository. Rationale and full list: docs/SECURITY.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# .env* is never committed. Only exception: .env.example with placeholders.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Supabase CLI state ------------------------------------------------
# Written by the CLI (version cache, link state). Never part of the repo:
# it can name a project ref, and this repository serves more than one.
supabase/.temp/

# --- Internal legacy data -------------------------------------------------
# These patterns are an extra brake, not a permission: the legacy project
# ../webpage is never copied into this repository in the first place.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
**/inventory.json
**/id_ledger.json
**/ebay.json
**/mappings/
images/master/
data/internal/

# --- Dependencies ---------------------------------------------------------
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# --- Next.js / build ------------------------------------------------------
/.next/
/out/
/build
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# --- Tests ----------------------------------------------------------------
/coverage

# --- Logs -----------------------------------------------------------------
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Deployment / tooling -------------------------------------------------
.vercel

# --- Editor artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
# nano writes <file>.save when an edit is aborted. Such a copy next to a
# migration is dangerous: it is a second, outdated version of a file that is
# meant to be executed exactly once.
*.save
*.swp
*~

# --- OS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Design sources. The shipped derivatives are committed — brand imagery in
# public/images/brand/, the card templates in public/images/cards/ — while the
# multi-megabyte originals stay out of the repository.
#
# `artwork/` moved to `designs/artwork/` on 2026-09-12, and the old rule was
# anchored at the root (`/artwork/`), so for a moment 15 MB of sources were
# neither ignored nor committed. Both folders are now named.
/designs/artwork/
/designs/cards/

# Local backups of production storage objects. Image bytes an administrator
# uploaded live in Supabase Storage, not in Git (ADR-0046); an export of them
# is a safety copy, not a repository asset.
/.backups/

# --- Business backups (ADR-0114) ------------------------------------------
# A downloaded business backup carries stock figures, purchase costs and the
# buyer names and addresses from the invoices — exactly the three kinds of
# data docs/SECURITY.md forbids in this repository. The file is meant to live
# on the owner's own disk, never here.
#
# Deliberately narrow: the file name is fixed by backupFileName() in
# src/lib/backup/document.ts, so the pattern can be. Ignoring `*.json`
# wholesale would silently swallow package.json, tsconfig.json and the
# curated data under data/.
#
# `backup-download.test.ts` keeps this rule from disappearing again.
skyisles-business-backup-*.json

# Dasselbe für die Plattformsicherung, und sie ist die schwerere: sie enthält
# zusätzlich das Auth-Inventar mit den E-Mail-Adressen aller Konten und die
# Storage-Dateien. Name fixiert durch platformArchiveFileName() in
# src/lib/backup/platform-archive.ts; `platform-archive.test.ts` hält diese
# Zeile fest.
skyisles-platform-backup-*.zip

# Local state of the staging UI fixtures (tools/ui-fixtures-ship-day.mts).
# Which throwaway sales exist right now is a fact about one machine.
.ui-fixtures-ship-day.json
tools/.ui-fixtures-ship-day.json
